    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 96.96, 524.113, 515.071, 573.321 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman9-Regular",
    "font size" : 8.966,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We prove that a pair of continuous disjoint periodic curves in C inscribes an isosceles trapezoid with any similarity type. The case of smooth curves can be identiﬁed with a Lagrangian intersection problem for a pair of Lagrangian cylinders in R × S1 × C, and the continuous case follows from the smooth one by a standard convergence argument."
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H1",
    "id" : 6,
    "level" : "Doctitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 257.04, 483.059, 355.346, 496.243 ],
    "heading level" : 1,
    "font" : "LMRoman12-Regular",
    "font size" : 14.346,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "1 Introduction"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 448.836, 540.052, 465.872 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Regular",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Let γ1,γ2: R → C be two continuous embeddings of the real line into C that satisfy the periodicity condition"
