    "bounding box" : [ 87.0, 232.263, 476.885, 242.912 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Regular",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Note that our deﬁnition depends on the order of the pair (γ1, γ2) unless Q is a rectangle."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 19,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 166.938, 540.058, 221.093 ],
    "font" : "LMRoman10-Italic",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Theorem 1.2. Suppose γ1 and γ2 are two continuous disjoint periodic embeddings of the real line into the plane, and suppose Q is an isosceles trapezoid. Then (γ1, γ2) admits a balanced inscription of Q. Furthermore, there is a generic subset of smooth disjoint periodic pairs such that each pair in this set admits at least two balanced inscriptions of Q that are not related under translation by √"
  }, {
    "type" : "image",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Figure",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 428.388, 176.868, 441.228, 177.348 ],
